      "math_academy_id": "e-5229",
      "problem": "The point $P$ with coordinates $(1, 0)$ lies on the curve $y = f(x) .$ What point must lie on $y=f(x + 1)+5?$",
      "worked_solution": "The graph of $y=f(x+1)+5$  is a translation of the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $1$ unit to the *left* and $5$ units up. So the $y$-coordinate increases by $5$ and the $x$-coordinate decreases by $1.$\n\nWe know that the point $P(1,0)$ lies on $y=f(x).$ Therefore, the point $(1-1,0+5) = (0,5)$ must lie on $y=f(x+1)+5.$",
